CLOUD REVIEWER seat for PR #2469 of tvofi/heatpump_optimizer, at head d2d361a449f0356f877e49a7ff59521f33739c37. Bus nonce: 0536df20a88febd26c99c2562b2d8147. Never send push notifications.
Setup: `git fetch --unshallow --tags origin`. The toolchain (venv python, node, gh) is on PATH from the environment. Run anything heavy in the background with Monitor and no timeout.
Role: read dev/governance/roles/fix-review.md and its rules from main, and follow them exactly. Fetch the PR head with `git fetch origin d2d361a449f0356f877e49a7ff59521f33739c37`; the PR body is in the PR. Verify each claim adversarially: mutate the fix and check the tests fail, and check every figure in the body at this head. Check that it merges with origin/main (`git merge-tree --write-tree`) and read CI on this head from the check-runs API.
Output: in a fresh directory of your own (`W=$(mktemp -d)`), write verdict.md, whose first line is exactly `Fix review: merge d2d361a449f0356f877e49a7ff59521f33739c37` or `Fix review: blocked d2d361a449f0356f877e49a7ff59521f33739c37 <class>: <reason>` (no brackets; the class is lower-case letters and dashes), in the format the role file gives, then a blank line, then `bus-nonce: 0536df20a88febd26c99c2562b2d8147`; put the evidence in `ev/` beside it. Do NOT run bus.sh: its dispatch record lives on the orchestrator's machine, which publishes the verdict there (cloud_relay.sh). Return the verdict on a probe ref, and push nothing else; this builds one parentless commit with a private index and touches no branch of your checkout: `R=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel); G=$(git rev-parse --absolute-git-dir); mkdir -p $W/pr && cp -r $W/verdict.md $W/ev $W/pr/ && cd $W/pr && T=$(GIT_DIR=$G GIT_INDEX_FILE=$W/idx GIT_WORK_TREE=$W/pr sh -c 'git add -A -f . && git write-tree') && C=$(GIT_DIR=$G git -c user.name=seat -c user.email=seat@users.noreply.github.com commit-tree $T -m "verdict 2469 d2d361a449f0356f877e49a7ff59521f33739c37") && git -C $R push -q origin $C:refs/heads/probe/rev-2469-0536df20`. That ref is the return signal. Do not post comments, approve or merge.
Never write to any branch except your return refs. Never work around a hook or a refusal; report it in your result instead.

Brief (snapshotted when this payload was rendered):
R10-UPDATE-PR-LOCK, the RCA fix for worktrees vanishing mid-prepr (2 incidents on 2026-10-19/20). Mechanism: update_pr.sh uses a fixed worktree $HPO_STATE_DIR/pr/upd-<branch> and force-removes it at start (update_pr.sh:35 at d1db05dfc); cloud_relay.sh pass's handoff arm (cloud_relay.sh:199-200) auto-runs update_pr.sh on the same branch as a manual run, so the second run deletes the first's live worktree. Fix: an exclusive per-branch lock on upd-<branch>.lock taken via python3 -I before any fetch or worktree change. A held lock prints BUSY and exits 75 with no change; other lock errors REFUSE; the push runs with the lock fd closed. cloud_relay.sh treats 75 as retry-next-pass, not failure. INSTRUMENTS.md documents the retry. Verify adversarially:
(1) the lock is taken before every mutation, including fetch, worktree remove/add and the log write, and released on every exit path and on SIGKILL (kernel-released);
(2) no child process inherits the lock fd;
(3) a stale lock file from a dead run does not block (null);
(4) exit 75 cannot mask a real failure in the relay;
(5) open_pr.sh and app_push.sh share no other fixed path that races the same way. If they do, it is a finding: fix or carry.
Re-run pr_args.sh --self-test (49/0 at head; 1 failed with main's update_pr), update_pr.sh --self-test and cloud_relay.sh --self-test (72/0), and mutate the # mut:lock line and the 75-handling line. The body wording was edited after the fixer's prepr: check every figure. Check whether R10-UPDATE-PR-LOCK is on main's roster: it was added on the roster branch at 04842e75 after #2467, so carry/record checks may read it as missing. If that blocks, name it.
